<title>INDIA: India's M3 money supply growth drops to 16.2 pct.</title>
<headline>India's M3 money supply growth drops to 16.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's year-on-year M3 money supply growth fell to 16.2 percent on November 22 from 16.4 percent a fortnight ago, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.  </p>
<p>		   M3 MONEY SUPPLY GROWTH (yr-on-yr in pct)</p>
<p>		   Nov 22, 1996    Nov 8, 1996  Nov 24, 1995</p>
<p>		   16.2		16.4	   13.97</p>
<p>Money supply was 6,539.87 billion rupees on November 22 compared to 6,547.11 billion rupees on November 8, 1996 and 5,613.40 billion on November 24, 1995, the RBI said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
